{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a stitch task (task #5498) from an automated code generation pipeline. The task is to implement srd076 requirements R3.2, R3.3, R4.1, R4.2 for `cmd/b2sum` (BLAKE2b checksum utility) in the go-unix-utils repository. This builds on prior tasks that implemented R1.1-R3.1. The specific requirements are:\n   - R3.2: `--tag` produces BSD tag format regardless of `-b`/`-t`\n   - R3.3: `--length=N` sets digest length in bits (positive multiple of 8, at most 512, default 512, exit 1 on invalid)\n   - R4.1: Exit 0 when all files processed and all verified digests match\n   - R4.2: Exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or checksum file unreadable\n   - R5: Add differential test cases covering R3.2, R3.3, R4.1, R4.2 using `testutils.RunDiffTests` against `gb2sum` reference binary\n\n   Acceptance criteria: go vet passes, go build succeeds, go test passes (or skips gracefully), all four requirements implemented, differential tests cover each requirement.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - BLAKE2b hash computation using `golang.org/x/crypto/blake2b`\n   - GNU vs BSD tag checksum output formats\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binary (`gb2sum`)\n   - `pkg/hashutil` shared library for hash computation, formatting, and verification\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for side-by-side binary comparison\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Variable-length BLAKE2b digests via `--length=N`\n   - Exit code contracts: 0 for success, 1 for any failure\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd076-b2sum.yaml** (READ)\n     - Contains full SRD for b2sum with requirements R1-R4\n     - R3.2: \"--tag produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t\"\n     - R3.3: \"--length=N sets the digest length in bits. N must be a positive multiple of 8 and at most 512. Default is 512. Must exit 1 with an error message if N is invalid.\"\n     - R4.1: \"Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match.\"\n     - R4.2: \"Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or the checksum file is unreadable.\"\n     - Non-goals: No BLAKE2s, no keyed hashing/MAC mode\n\n   - **cmd/b2sum/main.go** (READ - to be MODIFIED)\n     - Existing implementation covering R1.1-R3.1\n     - Has `parseArgs`, `parseLongFlag`, `parseLengthFlag`, `parseShortFlags` functions\n     - `options` struct with: binary, tag, check, warn, quiet, status, length fields\n     - Main function handles both digest and check modes\n     - Length validation: defaults to 512, validates positive multiple of 8, max 512\n     - Key observation: R3.2 (--tag) and R3.3 (--length) parsing infrastructure IS already present\n     - R4.1/R4.2 exit code logic IS already present in both check and digest paths\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         if opts.length == 0 { opts.length = 512 }\n         if opts.length <= 0 || opts.length%8 != 0 || opts.length > 512 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"b2sum: invalid length: %d\\n\", opts.length)\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         // ... builds HashConfig, handles check mode or digest mode\n         os.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go** (READ)\n     - Contains `ParseChecksumLine`, `VerifyChecksums`, `DigestFiles`, and helper functions\n     - `DigestFiles` handles both tag and non-tag output, returns exit code (0 or 1)\n     - `digestAndPrint` uses `FormatBSDTag` when tag=true (ignoring binary flag), `FormatGNU` otherwise\n     - `VerifyChecksums` reads checksum file, verifies each line, returns (allOK, error)\n     - `openInput` handles \"-\" as stdin\n\n   - **pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go** (NOT YET READ)\n     - Contains `HashConfig`, `CheckOptions` structs, `FormatGNU`, `FormatBSDTag`, `ComputeDigest` functions\n     - Referenced in package_contracts\n\n   - **cmd/b2sum/b2sum_test.go** (NOT YET READ - to be MODIFIED)\n     - Needs differential test cases for R3.2, R3.3, R4.1, R4.2\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was still in the reading/analysis phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Initial analysis suggests much of R3.2, R3.3, R4.1, R4.2 may already be functionally implemented in the existing code from prior tasks, since the flag parsing and exit code handling infrastructure is present. The main work appears to be:\n     1. Verifying edge cases are properly handled (e.g., --tag overriding -b/-t)\n     2. Potentially adding any missing edge case handling\n     3. Adding comprehensive differential test cases\n   - Need to read the test file to understand what test coverage already exists\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task specification with role, repository files, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, constraints, shared protocols, and package contracts. This is an automated stitch task from the cobbler orchestrator pipeline.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read `cmd/b2sum/b2sum_test.go` to understand existing test coverage\n   - Read `pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go` to understand FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ComputeDigest signatures\n   - Implement/verify R3.2 (--tag overrides -b/-t) in cmd/b2sum/main.go\n   - Implement/verif